  "description": "meme-id: goats_cant_talk_meme; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes an image of a large crowd of men, many wearing traditional Islamic headwear, with the text 'goats can't talk' at the top and 'why are so few muslim rapes reported?' at the bottom. This creates a false and degrading analogy, implying that because goats cannot speak, Muslim men are somehow incapable of reporting or being victims of sexual violence. This is a harmful and hateful stereotype that equates a religious group with animals, and it uses the image of a crowd of men to reinforce a false narrative about the prevalence or reporting of sexual assault within the Muslim community. The intent is to delegitimize the experiences of Muslim victims and to perpetuate Islamophobic tropes by suggesting that the community is inherently untruthful or unreporting due to cultural or religious reasons, rather than systemic barriers or social stigma. The meme is designed to provoke outrage or dismiss the seriousness of sexual violence against Muslims by framing it as a 'non-issue' based on a baseless and offensive comparison.",
